  "narrative": {
    "intro": "FCN is a federal contractor with $91.6M in contract obligations in FY2027 to date. FCN won 207 awards this fiscal year to date. FCN has an average award size of $442K. FCN obligations are down 90.0% year over year. FCN obligations in FY27 are a sharp step down from prior full fiscal years: FY26 totaled $918M, FY25 totaled $1B, FY24 totaled $995M, FY23 totaled $1B, and FY22 totaled $730M. FCN receives most of its FY2027 obligations from the Department of the Treasury, which obligated $82.7M to FCN. FCN sells primarily in the Other Computer Related Services market, where obligations to FCN total $91.5M so far in FY2027. FCN also shows smaller FY2027 obligations in Computer Systems Design Services and Computer Terminal and Other Computer Peripheral Equipment Manufacturing, with $82.9K and $0 respectively. FCN current-year totals are partial because fiscal year totals are reported to date, and the values listed for largest awards and expiring contracts represent total contract values rather than current-year obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has FCN revenue changed year over year?",
        "body": "FCN obligations fell 90.0% year over year. FCN FY27 obligations are $91.6M compared with $918M in FY26 and about $1B in FY25 and FY23. FCN obligations in FY24 were $995M and FCN obligations in FY22 were $730M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are FCN's top buyers and what does FCN sell?",
        "body": "FCN receives most FY2027 obligations from the Department of the Treasury, which obligated $82.7M. FCN also has obligations from the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau ($3.7M), the National Aeronautics and Space Administration ($2M), and smaller amounts across other agencies. FCN's largest market is Other Computer Related Services, with $91.5M in FY2027 obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
